===============================

The Lime parser generator itself is public domain (see LICENSE, distributed
under 0BSD). This file records upstream attribution for third-party material
bundled in the repository.


PostgreSQL-derived grammars
---------------------------

Several bundled grammars and grammar fragments are derived from PostgreSQL's
SQL grammar (`src/backend/parser/gram.y` and related scanner/keyword tables).
These derivatives include, but are not limited to:

  - contrib/oracle_compat/   (Oracle SQL dialect)
  - contrib/mysql_compat/    (MySQL dialect)
  - contrib/sqlite_compat/   (SQLite dialect)
  - contrib/duckdb_features/ (DuckDB dialect)
  - contrib/xml_query/       (XPath / XQuery)
  - examples/pg*             (PostgreSQL grammar / bootscanner examples)
  - the gram.y-derived grammars used in tests and benchmarks

